1c. document_template_extractions (touched by the existing FK)

    id uuid PK · document_id uuid NOT NULL · org_id uuid NOT NULL ·
    template_type text NOT NULL · extraction_source text NOT NULL ·
    raw_extraction jsonb · mapped_fields jsonb · reviewed_by uuid ·
    reviewed_at timestamptz · created_at timestamptz NOT NULL DEFAULT now()

    document_field_corrections.template_extraction_id -> dte(id), NULLABLE.
    Downstream it is used for exactly one thing: the kind='extraction' retrieval
    joins through it to reach dte.template_type ('k1') so K-1 corrections are
    scoped to the template. submit_field_correction also writes the corrected
    value back into dte.mapped_fields via jsonb_set in the same transaction, so
    the audit row and the live value never diverge. NULL means "not a template
    field correction" (i.e. a classification correction). Untouched by this
    sprint.

