TASK 2 — SCHEMA (additive)

  Applied exactly as specified, PLUS one deliberate addition:

   * document_id, org_id -> DROP NOT NULL (FKs retained)
   * ADD target_type text, target_id uuid
   * backfill ('document', document_id) — covered 0 rows, table was empty
   * both SET NOT NULL
   * document_field_corrections_target_type_chk:
       target_type IN ('document','note_terms','template_proposal')
   * document_field_corrections_document_pairing_chk:
       (target_type='document' AND document_id IS NOT NULL AND org_id IS NOT NULL)
       OR (target_type<>'document' AND org_id IS NULL)
   * CREATE INDEX idx_doc_field_corr_target (target_type, target_id)
   * NO FK on target_id (cannot span three tables). Reason recorded in a
     COMMENT ON COLUMN on target_id itself, per the sprint's instruction.

  *** THE ADDITION NOT IN THE SPRINT'S LITERAL DDL — and why ***
  A bare `target_type SET NOT NULL` with no default breaks EVERY existing
  writer listed in 1a; none of them mention the new columns. Fixing that by
  editing call sites is precisely the scope creep this sprint forbids. Instead:
     ALTER COLUMN target_type SET DEFAULT 'document'
     + BEFORE INSERT trigger document_field_corrections_default_target_trg
       -> NEW.target_id := NEW.document_id, ONLY when target_id IS NULL
          AND target_type = 'document'
  An explicitly supplied target_id is never rewritten, so polymorphic writers
  are unaffected. Result: every pre-existing INSERT statement stays byte-for-byte
  valid and lands correctly typed. ZERO call sites were modified.

  RLS — both shapes coexist
    UNCHANGED: document_field_corrections_org_isolation (as quoted in 1a).
    ADDED, all scoped to target_type <> 'document':
      document_field_corrections_global_read           FOR SELECT
      document_field_corrections_global_super_admin_insert  FOR INSERT
      document_field_corrections_global_super_admin_update  FOR UPDATE
      document_field_corrections_global_super_admin_delete  FOR DELETE
    All five policies are PERMISSIVE, so they OR together. A 'document' row
    scores false on global_read and is therefore still governed solely by the
    org predicate -> cross-org invisibility arithmetically unchanged. A
    'note_terms' row scores true -> globally readable. Both asserted live under
    the real non-bypass app_service role (verify assertion 8).


